doc:Factsarticle1_115 schema:abstract "Model-agnostic meta-learning coupled with digital twins is applied to predictive maintenance of robotic arms in assembly lines. An ensemble-based meta-learning approach integrates majority voting, while operational grouping uses Latin hypercube sampling to improve few-shot learning and generalization. The methodology is validated using a synthetic vibration signal dataset of robotic arm faults." .
